      <guid>http://localhost:1313/journals/first-journals/week-1/nandini/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;journal-byline&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;span&gt;🔬&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/members/nandini-dasar/&#34;&gt;Nandini Dasar&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;  · Researcher &amp;amp; Documentation Intern&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;journal-byline-back&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/journals/first-journals/week-1/&#34;&gt;← First Journals · Week 1&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🔬 Nandini Dasar&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;-nandini-dasar&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#-nandini-dasar&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Weekly Progress Report: Week 1&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;weekly-progress-report-week-1&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#weekly-progress-report-week-1&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Classroom Observation &amp;amp; Research · Researcher&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h4 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;1. Executive Overview &amp;amp; Key Focus&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;1-executive-overview--key-focus&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#1-executive-overview--key-focus&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h4&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;During Week 1, I began my work as a researcher and classroom observer on a project about how children learn best. My role was to watch closely, listen carefully, and step in only when needed to understand each student&amp;rsquo;s learning difficulties and responses. I observed sessions taught by Teacher Zaveriya, noting how students took part, paid attention, understood ideas, and communicated their answers. Students arrived with very different levels of prior knowledge: some grasped concepts quickly, while others needed repeated explanations and simple examples.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
